<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31976" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ob-torpesco</span></b> , pŭi, 3,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch.
			n.</i>, <i>to become numb</i> or <i>stiff; to be benumbed</i>, <i>become
			insensible</i>, <i>lose feeling.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">torpedo . . . piscium qui securi supernatantes
					obtorpuere, corripiens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 42, 67, § 143</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manus prae metu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					22, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Dom. 52, 135</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oculi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Contr. 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">squamae,</span>”
				<i>grow hard</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 27, 41, § 99</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subactus miseriis obtorpui, Cic. poët.
					Tusc. 3, 28, 67: circumfuso undique pavore, ita obtorpuit,
					ut, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					34, 38 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obtorpuerunt quodammodo animi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					32, 20, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
